WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.219
INTRO:
In early April, Elon surprised the world when

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:07.229
he announced that he had acquired a 9.2% stake
in Twitter.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:11.760
At first, he played it cool and didn’t make
it clear whether he wanted to buy the company

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.000
or not.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.930
Many speculated that Elon was just trying
to join the Twitter board so that he could

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.430
influence decisions at the company without
taking over the entire company.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.960
The fact that Twitter capped his stake at
15% just made it even less likely that Elon

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.610
would attempt a takeover.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:32.430
But, despite all that, it didn’t take long
for Elon to make a buyout offer for $41.39

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.430
billion.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.109
And board would eventually accept a bid for
$44 billion.

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:42.249
Elon instantly went ahead and sold off his
Tesla stock and secured billions of dollars

00:00:42.249 --> 00:00:43.789
worth of loans to pay for Twitter.

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:48.999
All of this unfolded within a month, so it
seemed like both Elon and Twitter wanted to

00:00:48.999 --> 00:00:50.249
get this deal done ASAP.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:54.929
But, at this point, it’s been nearly 2 months
since Elon secured funding for the Twitter

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:58.230
deal, and we’ve seen virtually no progress.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:02.559
Not to mention, Twitter stock hasn’t been
doing that great either which is not the best

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:03.639
of signs.

00:01:03.639 --> 00:01:07.600
If Elon’s deal does end up taking place,
he’d be buying each share of Twitter for

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.770
$54.20.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:14.280
So, buying Twitter shares under this price
is basically just free profit as long as the

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.280
deal goes through.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:21.590
But, right now, Twitter stands at just $39.41
meaning that you’d profit 37% if the deal

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.719
goes through at the original price.

00:01:23.719 --> 00:01:27.020
Given that the stock has sold off so much
though, it doesn’t look like the market

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.070
is super confident that the deal will end
up taking place atleast not at the original

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.070
price.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.170
So, what happened to Elon’s Twitter deal?

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:42.509
FAKE ACCOUNTS:
Starting off with the most noted concern,

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:45.770
Elon is worried about how many fake accounts
are on Twitter.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.040
In terms of fake accounts, we have two main
categories which are inactive accounts and

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.700
spam bots.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.310
Inactive accounts are self explanatory.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.249
These are accounts that were created years
ago, and the user has since stopped using

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:59.899
Twitter or they have switched to another account.

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:04.549
But this is not what Elon is really talking
about, his primary concern with fake accounts

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:06.119
is spambots.

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:08.890
Us YouTube people are extremely familiar with
these.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.860
There’s probably some crypto expert in the
comments section down below named Mary Jane

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.210
who 40 people are willing to vouch for.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:19.290
Such spammers are generally account for an
extremely small portion of social media.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.580
However, given that each spammer operates
30 to 50 accounts, they actually make up a

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.660
decent amount of the total accounts.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.690
Twitter says that fake accounts make up less
than 5% of their daily active users, but being

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.030
an avid Twitter user himself, Elon isn’t
quite convinced.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.880
But, what’s the big deal with fake accounts
anyway?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.580
Sure, they’re a slight nuisance and it’s
a shame that people fall for these scams,

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.530
but it’s not worth halting an entire acquisition
over right?

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.410
Well, Elon thinks it is for a few reasons
starting with the company’s business model.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.910
Twitter makes money be selling ad slots on
their platform just like most other social

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:53.910
media platforms.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.340
But, if 10 or 20% of Twitter accounts are
just bots, advertisers would be wasting a

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.370
significant number of impressions on useless
accounts.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.430
This would in turn lead to lower conversion
rates which would lead to less advertisers

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:08.260
wanting to market on Twitter and eventually
less revenue for Twitter.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.930
Aside from less ad revenue, bots also ruin
Twitter’s credibility.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.880
Elon wants to make Twitter into this super
righteous place where free speech is supported

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.250
and people can engage in intellectual discussions
about social issues.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.940
But, people won’t exactly be enthused to
do this if a bunch of the platform is just

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.940
bots.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:29.210
So, for Elon, dealing with the fake accounts
is a matter of protecting Twitter’s credibility

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:33.830
amongst advertisers and users, and consequently,
he’s taking it pretty seriously.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.690
Elon has requested a detailed report that
goes through how Twitter is determining how

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.830
many bots there are, but Twitter has been
reluctant to hand over these details.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.810
The most likely reason for this is that they
simply don’t have the details or they’re

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.280
not confident about the details that they
do have.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:53.790
Twitter’s CEO, Parag, was pretty upfront
about how it’s extremely challenging to

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.820
differentiate between legit accounts with
seemingly suspicious activity and spam accounts

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.660
with seemingly legitimate activity.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.490
So, more likely than not, Twitter has been
scrambling to find more evidence to support

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.540
their claims before they hand over a more
detailed report to Elon.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:12.090
Honestly, I don’t think Elon would cancel
the deal over bots, but if there are more

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:16.090
bots than Twitter initially claimed, Elon
may try to use this as a negotiating point

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.160
to drive down the acquisition price.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.720
FINANCING CONTINGENCIES:
Though Elon has secured most of the funding

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.030
required to buy Twitter, he doesn’t quite
have it all.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:31.460
At the time of making this video, Elon has
committed to paying $33.5 billion in cash

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.880
and he has secured $7.1 billion worth of equity
based financing.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:40.030
But, this only adds about to $40.6 billion
meaning that he’s still $3.4 billion short

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.110
from the $44 billion acquisition price.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:46.570
Elon has vaguely stated that the remaining
amount will also come from various loans,

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.120
but the specifics have yet to be finalized.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.870
At one point, he was in talks with a group
of private equity firms to raise $2 to $3

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:53.870
billion.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.340
But, this wasn’t to make up for the disparity.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.140
This was to reduce the amount of cash Elon
would have to put up.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:04.320
Maybe Elon’s goal is to shave down the acquisition
price by 10% and pay no more than $40 billion

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.320
for Twitter.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.460
Aside from not securing the final amount,
Elon has become much more cautious when it

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.430
comes to equity based financing.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:15.030
In May, he was working on getting a $12.5
billion margin loan based on his Tesla stock,

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.190
but he has since scrapped the idea.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.520
This is likely due to the stock market and
Tesla stock getting crushed since he made

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.770
the deal with Twitter.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.470
Since April, Tesla stock has sold of 45%.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:28.889
To make things worse, it seems like Elon is
forecasting some potentially painful quarters

00:05:28.889 --> 00:05:30.350
to come for Tesla.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.990
Recently, he announced plans for laying off
10% of their salaried workforce.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:38.520
He’s also been talking about how GigaTexas
and GigaBerlin are currently gigantic money

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.810
furnaces because they can’t get enough parts
to ramp up production.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.870
Elon has even started mentioning worries regarding
bankruptcy.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.050
Now, I don’t think Tesla is in any risk
of going bankrupt in the imminent future.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:54.140
But based on everything Elon has been saying,
it looks like Tesla is likely in for some

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.700
painful quarters which could drive the stock
price lower.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:01.340
And the last thing that Elon would want is
to get margin called at the bottom.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.880
So, it’s not surprising that he’s being
a lot more cautious when it comes to equity

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:05.880
based financing.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.710
Elon’s not the only one with second thoughts
either.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:09.710
The banks that offered to finance his debt
have also put the deal on hold.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.270
The banks are fearful that credit investors
wont buy the debt as long as Elon is fighting

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.790
with Twitter regarding the fake accounts.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.840
So, they’re waiting for the uncertainty
to subside before they actually put together

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:18.840
the required funds.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:23.230
They’re technically not allowed to do this
because the deal is technically still on.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.900
And Twitter can actually take the banks to
court for not meeting their funding obligations.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.010
But, the general consensus is that it’s
very unlikely that Twitter would actually

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.610
waste money on taking these guys to court.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.070
After all, if Elon calls off the deal, it’s
not like the funding would be that useful

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.070
anyway.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:41.919
So, Twitter’s best bet is to just convince
Elon that the fake accounts are a negligible

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:45.980
issue or to simply settle for a lower purchase
price.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:51.080
APPROVAL:
The points that we’ve discussed so far are

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.860
completely under Elon’s control.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:57.449
At any point, he could just decide to proceed
despite the fake accounts.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:01.740
And as for the financing, he could just sell
off some more Tesla stock if he really needed

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:02.740
to.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:05.690
But, even if Elon was willing to do this,
it’s not like he could complete the deal

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.949
right now anyway because there are external
factors that are out of his control.

00:07:09.949 --> 00:07:13.919
First of all, we have the HSR Act or the Hart-Scott-Rodino
Act.

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:18.390
Like with any piece of legislation, the HSR
act has a bunch of stipulations and conditions.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:22.750
But, the part that applies to the Twitter
deal is the 30 day waiting period.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:26.560
Whenever a merger or acquisition of a certain
magnitude is proposed, the deal has to be

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.040
reviewed by the Federal Trade Commission and
the US Department of Justice.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:34.460
These institutions then have 30 days to review
the deal and either do nothing which is basically

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.200
equivalent to approving it, or they can request
more information.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:42.130
Just because the request more information
doesn’t mean that a deal is dead per se.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:45.700
But, this would delay the deal by months if
not years.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.440
Usually, they’re just looking to stop monopolies
from forming.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:53.500
For example, they wouldn’t want Shell and
Exxon to join or Boeing and Airbus to join.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:57.770
Within the social media scene, they might
not want Facebook and Twitter to join, but

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.360
Elon doesn’t own any other social media
companies.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:05.699
Tesla’s a car company and SpaceX is a rocket
company, so there’s really no risk of forming

00:08:05.699 --> 00:08:07.770
some sort of social media monopoly.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:12.540
Something that may concern them is how much
power this deal would give Elon, but I don’t

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.449
think that this would be a gamechanger either.

00:08:14.449 --> 00:08:17.860
I mean, just take a look at how much power
Mark Zuckerberg has.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:22.710
Even including the bots, Twitter only has
330 million monthly active users which is

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.870
an insane amount, but only a fraction of Facebook.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:30.250
WhatsApp alone has over 2 billion monthly
active users while Instagram has another 2

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.250
billion monthly active users.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:34.860
And given that the government hasn’t yet
broken apart Facebook, I don’t think they

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:35.860
would put up much resistance.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:41.599
Not to mention, the 30 days have already passed,
so it looks the deal is good to go from a

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:43.269
regulation standpoint.

00:08:43.269 --> 00:08:46.779
Elon and Twitter do still need a few more
government approvals, but this was really

00:08:46.779 --> 00:08:48.980
the main hurdle regulation wise.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:52.540
Even after all of this though, there is still
one more hurdle that the Twitter deal has

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.730
to jump over, and that’s shareholder approval.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:58.100
At the end of the day, Twitter is a public
company, so public shareholders do have a

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.930
say in what happens to the company.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.470
Twitter hasn’t yet revealed what date the
voting will take place, but it’s expected

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:06.240
to happen in late July or early August.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.449
Many shareholders do have concerns regarding
Elon taking over the company.

00:09:09.449 --> 00:09:13.130
But, the general consensus is that the shareholders
will approve the deal.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:17.290
And once they do, it’s just a matter of
actually completing the deal.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:22.290
BACKING AWAY:
Something that we haven’t discussed so far

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:27.170
is what happens if Elon backs away from the
deal, and the reason for this is that he can’t

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.529
really back away.

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:33.480
First of all, Elon will have to pay a $1 billion
breakup fee, but that’s the least of his

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.480
concerns.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:37.680
Unless it’s revealed that Twitter is a ponzi
scheme or something, Twitter will have rights

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:41.720
to sue Elon for breaching contract, and they
could easily launch a multi-billion dollar

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.490
lawsuit against him.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:48.130
Not only would this be a massive hassle, but
it would be a permanent stain on his reputation.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.699
And let’s be real here.

00:09:49.699 --> 00:09:54.519
Do you really think that he bought 9% of Twitter,
sold $8.5 billion worth of Tesla stock, secured

00:09:54.519 --> 00:09:59.240
a bunch of funding, and made a $44 billion
offer just to walk away due to bots that he

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:00.920
was already aware of?

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:06.089
That makes no sense whatsoever, these are
all moves of a serious buyer and the bot thing

00:10:06.089 --> 00:10:08.019
is really just a negotiation tactic.

00:10:08.019 --> 00:10:12.411
It may actually help him shave off a few billion
from the acquisition price, but we’ll just

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:13.411
have to wait and see.

00:10:13.411 --> 00:10:17.240
In the meantime, he’s looking to minimize
his margin risk and ensure that the Twitter

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.459
deal won’t screw over his Tesla stake.

00:10:19.459 --> 00:10:23.339
And given that the shareholder vote doesn’t
have to take place till October 24, Elon and

00:10:23.339 --> 00:10:25.730
Twitter have plenty of time to figure this
out.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:30.220
And chances are, I think they will figure
it out and that the deal will take place probably

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:33.389
by the end of this year, but that’s just
what I think.

00:10:33.389 --> 00:10:35.649
Do you think the Twitter deal will go through?

